# CapitalForge Git Workflow

## Branch Naming

```
<type>/<feature-id>-<short-description>
```

| Type | Use | Example |
|------|-----|---------|
| `feature/` | New functionality | `feature/F-001-multiplier-strategy` |
| `fix/` | Bug fixes | `fix/F-007-bucket-decrement` |
| `docs/` | Documentation only | `docs/pos-operating-system` |
| `refactor/` | No behavior change | `refactor/allocation-extract-recalc` |
| `chore/` | Tooling, deps | `chore/upgrade-prisma` |
| `test/` | Test additions | `test/strategy-excel-parity` |

**Rules:**
- Branch from latest `main`
- One feature/fix per branch
- Keep branches short-lived (< 1 week)

## Commit Naming

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

[optional body]
```

| Type | Use |
|------|-----|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation |
| `refactor` | Code restructure, no behavior change |
| `test` | Tests |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

**Examples:**
```
feat(strategy): use multiplier-based buy amounts
fix(transaction): reverse bucket usage on delete
docs(pos): add project operating system
refactor(allocation): extract recalculateBuckets helper
test(strategy): add Excel parity unit tests
```

**Rules:**
- Imperative mood ("add" not "added")
- Max 72 chars for subject line
- Reference feature ID in body if applicable: `Closes F-001`

## PR Naming

```
[F-0XX] Brief description of change
```

**Examples:**
```
[F-001] Multiplier-based strategy rules
[F-003] Remove JWT auth bypass middleware
[docs] Add project operating system
```

## PR Requirements

Before opening PR:
```
□ Branch up to date with main
□ Focused diff — one feature/fix
□ FEATURE_BACKLOG.md updated
□ TIME_LOG.md entry added
□ DECISION_LOG.md updated (if architectural)
□ Backend: lint + build + test pass
□ Frontend: lint + build pass
□ Manual test steps in PR description
□ No secrets committed
```

## PR Description Template

```markdown
## Summary
[1-2 sentences: what and why]

## Feature
F-0XX — [Feature name from backlog]

## Test plan
- [ ] [Specific step]
- [ ] [Another step]

## Screenshots
[If UI change]
```

## Merge Strategy

- **Default:** Squash merge to `main`
- **One PR = one commit** on main (clean history)
- Delete branch after merge
- No force push to `main`
- No merge commits unless multi-PR feature (rare)

## Release Tagging

```
v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>.<PATCH>
```

| Bump | When |
|------|------|
| MAJOR | Breaking API or data model |
| MINOR | New features, backward compatible |
| PATCH | Bug fixes only |

**Release steps:**
1. Update `RELEASE_NOTES.md`
2. Merge all PRs to `main`
3. `git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z`
4. Deploy backend (Render auto) + frontend (Vercel auto)
5. Run `prisma migrate deploy` if schema changed
6. Verify `/api/health`

## What NOT to Do

- Force push to `main`
- Commit directly to `main` (use branches)
- Combine unrelated changes in one PR
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) unless explicitly needed
- Commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets
- Amend pushed commits
- Update git config

## Documentation Updates in PRs

| File | When Required |
|------|---------------|
| `TIME_LOG.md` | Every PR |
| `FEATURE_BACKLOG.md` | Feature/fix PRs |
| `DECISION_LOG.md` | Architectural changes |
| `API_CONTRACTS.md` | API changes |
| `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` | Bug fixes (remove/mark resolved) |
| `RELEASE_NOTES.md` | Release PRs |
